## Literature search: walking speed in human-motion latent spaces

The topic has close prior work, so the strongest contribution is **not simply showing that walking speed relates to a latent representation**. Prior studies already generate gaits at specified speeds, encode speed in learned gait latents, or edit motion timing. The more specific question in your note—whether a **single post-hoc linear direction** changes **measured physical forward speed** in decoded human motion while preserving style and plausibility—still looks like a focused, testable gap.

